# .spun update with dir001 and @APP@ in spun.cat, both older than on the
# server. dir001 is first and goes to its directory in spun.cat, never to the
# publisher's suggestion; its DIRTEST.TXT exists, so C at the Overwrite
# question cancels it. Cancel stops the whole update, so @APP@ is not updated
# either. mame-dir.sh checks that spun.cat and dir001's files are as they
# were. The error ends .spun, so ON ERROR keeps the autoexec running, as in
# spun-dir-cancel.scn.in: the handler prints SPUNERR with the error code and
# the line of .spun (30). It has no noreset for the reason given there.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
put @UPDCAT@ /sys/spun.cat
put @OLD@ /apps/spundir/deep/DIRTEST.TXT
autostart ON ERROR ERROR TO e,l:PRINT "SPUNERR ";e;" ";l:FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
autostart .spun update
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 40
key 16 c
snap 15 20 25 39
screen 39 Overwrite C:/apps/spundir/deep/
screen 39 SPUNERR 255 30
